{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1564962-making-sleepwalkers","id":1564962,"title":"Making Sleepwalkers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-25T13:23:35-07:00","id":1564962,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Making Sleepwalkers","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> What stops a Mystery Cult Initiation to have benefits that make you sleepwalker directly? <b>Fitful Slumber</b> or <b>Sleepwalker</b>, either merit would grant you the status, and I might be wrong but seems either is allowed even at first level (if not at first level, then the 3rd and onwards can get you supernatural merits).<br /> <br /> If there was a reliable way to make someone sleepwalker why mages are not working on this? (except that p. 303 of the Core says that no one knows how to make people Sleepwalkers).<br /> <br /> The mechanics of the cult, I was imagining something like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mystery Cult Initiation (Hypnopompic Circle)</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Rating</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Rank</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Description</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Initiate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Meditative Mind 1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Apprentice</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Meditative Mind 2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Disciple</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Meditative Mind 4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Adept</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fitful Slumber, High Speech Perception or Lucid Dreamer</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Master</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Astral Adept</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> Essentially you make them better at resisting breaking points (<b>Meditative Mind 4</b> so they get the +1 bonus to breaking points faster and easier), then you expose them to the Supernal enough times they get accostumed to it (<b>Fitful Slumber</b> and <b>High Speech Perception</b>), and eventually they reach the Astral Realms (<b>Astral Adept</b>, and if they have used <b>Meditative Mind 2</b>, they get a +3 bonus to the Resolve + Composure roll to enter the Astral). You could change for <b>Lucid Dreamer</b> and it still would fit the themes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mechanically and thematically makes sense, there is a whole sequence there... But feels weird that this is possible, if a bit hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-25-2026, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T13:40:19-07:00","id":1564963,"title":"","content":"Nothing stops them, but they need to delve into it enough to gain a supernatural merit at 3 dots. Cryptopolies and Labyrinths can operate on that idea. First few levels are filters, higher levels are where supernatural secrets dwell, either to recruit Sleepwalker allies or attemptimg to nudge potential candidates into Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T18:57:35-07:00","id":1564969,"title":"","content":"Remember that a Mystery Cult is more than just a mechanical merit structure. It's a <i>mystery cult,</i> with <i>secret teachings</i> and an <i>occult relic.</i> In order to make this cult, a character is going to need to acquire a method of accomplishing this and/or have an item of power that does this.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like asking a homeless person why he couldn't just use the Resources Merit to acquire housing. Just because there's no mechanical gate preventing a Merit purchase doesn't mean that narratively you can just <i>do</i> that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T19:11:40-07:00","id":1564970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1564962-making-sleepwalkers?p=1564969#post1564969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that a Mystery Cult is more than just a mechanical merit structure. It's a <i>mystery cult,</i> with <i>secret teachings</i> and an <i>occult relic.</i> In order to make this cult, a character is going to need to acquire a method of accomplishing this and/or have an item of power that does this.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like asking a homeless person why he couldn't just use the Resources Merit to acquire housing. Just because there's no mechanical gate preventing a Merit purchase doesn't mean that narratively you can just <i>do</i> that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah you are right. There is the justification of the relic/mechanics.<br /> <br /> I was thinking as a Mage aiming for the result: make them mentally and spiritually stronger (Meditative Mind 4) and expose them to the Supernal until they can accept it (Fitful Slumber, High Speech Perception). <br /> <br /> Even outside the cult, the reasoning seems solid, if abusive. But again mages, it seems something that Mysterium, Silver Ladder and Free Council would be interested in, but Thearchs and Libertines would have to be either heretical or very obsessed to suffer such abuse of sleeeprs for the goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-25T22:03:44-07:00","id":1564973,"title":"","content":"As you say, the core suggests that there is no known straightforward procedure to <i>just</i> make someone a Sleepwalker, which is a suggestion that something like this would not work. Something that worked would be more involved than this. Somebody would have tried this already.<br /> <br /> However, there <i>are</i> plenty of ways to make someone a sleepwalker, if you don't mind also making them <i>something else.</i> Giving somebody an inborn Supernatural Merit makes them a sleepwalker. Making somebody a vampiric ghoul makes them a sleepwalker. Triggering the Divergence makes someone a sleepwalker. Some of these methods would be within the grasp of a Mystery Cult.<br /> <br /> Would that be ethical? Probably not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T05:38:24-07:00","id":1564977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1564962-making-sleepwalkers#post1564962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there was a reliable way to make someone sleepwalker why mages are not working on this? (except that p. 303 of the Core says that no one knows how to make people Sleepwalkers).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're answering your own question there.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the strict wording of the rules, I think some common sense needs to be applied as to what Merits make sense as the kind of thing that might come out of membership in a secretive group.<br /> <br /> That said, even for those created and controlled by mages, Mystery Cults should probably be seen in terms that are more sophisticated than a basic application of their Merit rules imply, and more organic than an idea that a mage purpose built them towards every little capability they possess. The more elaborate explanation of what makes them in the Chronicles core book might get at that; that from the side of the mages, they still had to develop something with Purpose, Relic and Doctrine, and the Merits they acquire grew out of that rather than mages just defining Merits they want and training people towards them.<br /> <br /> In any case, I would say it's valid for a given Mystery Cult to have Sleepwalker as a perk of membership, and the mages in control don't understand why, have been unable to replicate it, and the particulars of membership don't really work for using the same cult en masse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-26T06:44:44-07:00","id":1564980,"title":"","content":"Yep, apart from your Relic, you also need to figure out what draws people to it, what makes them stay, what are you offering them. An example is that while delving into the Astral works at high tier, you need to consider the steps to get there. What promise are you making so they see it as more than meditation class ? How are you showing its worth sticking around ? The cult of Mammon from the CofD book has an easy one, its a secret club of old money and networking, stick around and you too share in that wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}